`_unwrap` is a public property on `ConfigFile` with no TypeScript `private` modifier (defined at `code/core/src/csf-tools/ConfigFile.ts:178`). The `(config as any)` cast is unnecessary, and more critically, the `typeof ... === 'function'` guard creates a silent fallback to `node.declaration` without TS-assertion unwrapping. If that fallback fires, files like `export default defineMain({}) as StorybookConfig` will NOT be detected as already-transformed — `node.declaration` would be a `TSAsExpression`, causing `t.isCallExpression(declaration)` to return `false`, so `isAlreadyTransformed` is `false` and the codemod re-processes already-correct code. The rest of this function (line 145 in Scenario 2) already calls `config._unwrap(node.declaration as t.Node)` directly without any cast — match that pattern:
```typescript
// eslint-disable-next-line no-underscore-dangle
const declaration = config._unwrap(node.declaration);
```
